وضعیت تجاری‌سازی محصول', '(Maximum 200 words)
The DCIM (Data Center Infrastructure Management) Control and Monitoring System developed by Fan Tadbir Sabz Vira delivers a comprehensive, unified platform for real-time monitoring and intelligent control of all critical components within a data center environment. To date, this solution has been successfully deployed in more than 30 large-scale data centers across 19 provinces, demonstrating proven reliability and scalability.
By seamlessly integrating the monitoring and control of electrical, mechanical, environmental, and physical security subsystems alongside IT and system infrastructure, the platform significantly reduces operational risk and cost while improving overall system efficiency and service continuity.
Designed as a standards-compliant, high-availability, and secure DCIM solution, the system is modular, scalable, and fully customizable to meet the specific requirements of Tier II and Tier III data centers. It supports both physical infrastructure management and IT infrastructure management, including asset management, capacity planning, energy management, change management, network connectivity, forecasting, business intelligence (BI), data analytics, and advanced 2D/3D real-time visualization.
The electrical module enables intelligent power capacity management, power quality analysis, real-time energy consumption visualization, trend analysis, efficiency assessment, PUE calculation, and early detection of potential issues to prevent service disruption. The mechanical module dynamically optimizes airflow and cooling performance based on real-time IT load, ensuring maximum availability and reliability of cooling infrastructure.
The platform supports a wide range of environmental sensors—including temperature, humidity, dust, water leakage, door status, smoke, heat detection, lighting, motion detection, fluid level and flow rate, air and water pressure—whose data is centrally analyzed and visualized. Integration with fire detection and suppression systems, access control, and CCTV further enhances comprehensive data center visibility and security.
Features and Advantages:
(Maximum 100 words)
Unified monitoring, control, and management of data center physical infrastructure (DCIM)
Fully multi-vendor / brand-agnostic architecture
Integrated subsystems:
Electrical: MV/LV, UPS, Generators, PDUs
Mechanical: Chillers, CRAC, InRow units, Pumps
Environmental: Temperature, Humidity, Leak Detection, Dust, Motion
Physical Security: CCTV, Access Control, Fire Detection & Suppression
Support for standard industrial protocols
Customizable scenario and automation engine
Online setpoint definition and application
Manual / Automatic equipment operation modes
Intelligent alarm management with prioritization
Event & log management system
Trend analysis, historical data, and reporting
Automated PUE calculation
Data center health map
Advanced 2D and 3D visualization
Modular and phased implementation support
Designed for Tier II / Tier III data centers
Operational Benefits:
-Reduced downtime and increased service availability
-Proactive fault detection before critical incidents occur
-Reduced dependency on operators and minimized human error
-Extended lifespan of electrical and cooling equipment
-Faster troubleshooting and reduced MTTR (Mean Time to Repair)
Economic Benefits:
-Reduced energy costs through dynamic optimization
-Maximum utilization of infrastructure assets
-Lower maintenance and operational expenses
-Prevention of costly damages caused by leaks, fire, or thermal issues
Management Benefits:
-A true Single Pane of Glass for the entire data center
-Data-driven operational and strategic decision-making
-Executive and analytical reporting over defined time periods
-Readiness for transition toward Green Data Centers
Strategic Advantages:
-Independence from foreign brands and vendors
-Long-term scalability across the data center lifecycle
-Adaptability to diverse data center architectures
-Ideal for mission-critical and high-availability environments
