1790701111250', 'SmartCTL is an advanced industrial controller designed to collect, process, and manage data from a wide range of equipment and sensors. As a core component of SCADA-based control and monitoring systems, it enables real-time monitoring of generators, chillers, cooling systems, UPS units, batteries, motors, power meters, and a wide variety of environmental sensors—including temperature, humidity, air quality, water leakage, dust, pressure, liquid level, differential pressure, and water flow rate.
In addition to data acquisition and storage, SmartCTL is capable of issuing control commands, such as equipment on/off switching, automated parameter adjustments, and execution of predefined control scenarios. The device features both digital and analog inputs for environmental and operational data acquisition and supports Modbus RTU and Modbus TCP communication protocols for seamless integration with other systems. Its digital outputs enable precise equipment control based on predefined conditions.
SmartCTL is an ideal solution for intelligent monitoring and control across diverse industries and can be seamlessly integrated with virtually all control and monitoring platforms available on the market.
The device consists of two independent modules:
Gateway:
Acts as a web server supporting Ethernet, Modbus TCP, SNMP, and Modbus RTU communication.
Data Logger:
Enables direct connection of various digital and analog sensors.
The Data Logger can also function as an extension module via Modbus RTU, allowing connectivity to controllers from different vendors and fulfilling the requirements of complex monitoring and control systems.
SmartCTL is widely used for environmental control, power infrastructure monitoring, and cooling system supervision in large data centers, performance monitoring of industrial facilities and factories, electrical consumption monitoring and control within energy management systems, and deployment in smart buildings. The product is available in 1U and 2U rack-mounted models.
Features and Advantages:
High Sensor Connectivity
Supports 24 to 72 digital inputs/outputs or up to 100 temperature and humidity sensors
Achieved through proprietary board development, optimized hardware design, enhanced communication protocols, noise filtering modules, and fault detection algorithms
High System Integration (Embedded + System Integration)
Custom-designed boards with onboard processors
Elimination of off-the-shelf modules
Fully localized hardware enabling all processing on a single board
High Measurement Accuracy
Reduced manufacturing and design tolerances
Automatic calibration algorithms
Advanced data correction techniques
Noise-resistant circuit design
High Reliability in Harsh Environments
Rugged industrial-grade design
Protective electronic board coatings to minimize electromagnetic interference
Real-Time Processing & Big Data Handling
Optimized firmware architecture
Reduced processing latency
RTOS-based real-time performance
Advanced Hardware & Software Security
Encryption mechanisms
Authentication and role-based access control
Protection against data tampering at both hardware and software levels
Technical Specifications:
Digital I/O: 24 to 72 digital inputs or outputs
Analog Inputs: 16 to 48 analog inputs
PWM Outputs: 24 to 72 PWM outputs
Internal Storage: 16 GB internal memory for sensor data logging
Communications & Networking: 4 to 8 independent Modbus RTU rings
Communication Protocols: Modbus RTU،Modbus TCP،SNMP،CAN FD support (new generation design)
Wireless Communication: Optional wireless activation for sensor data collection upon customer request
Data Access: Sensor data available via Modbus TCP and SNMP
Full MIB file support: SNMP versions v1 / v2c / v3
Web Server Configuration: IP managementTime ،server configuration،Mail server configuration
Web Security: User management and access security،HTTPS communication
Security Certificates: SSL key support
Firmware Update: Firmware upgrade via webserver
Ports RJ45: 8 to 24 ports
Phoenix connector: Modbus RTU and power supply
Network ports: Ethernet, Modbus TCP, SNMP
Power Supply:220V AC, 50/60 Hz
Enclosure:Metal (steel) housing with anti-static, textured powder coating
Installation:1U (S1 series) and 2U (S2 series)
Rack-mountable for telecom and server racks
Form Factor:1U / 2U rack mount
