26479521907500', 'SmartPMS is a smart, multi-channel power monitoring system designed for precise measurement, monitoring, and analysis of electrical parameters and power quality. By detecting electrical anomalies in real time, it helps prevent outages and protects critical equipment from damage.
With a strong focus on energy management, SmartPMS identifies high-consumption points, inefficiencies, and energy losses within electrical infrastructures, playing a vital role in optimizing consumption and reducing operational costs.
Designed as a Multi-Circuit Power Monitoring System, SmartPMS is available in 3, 8, and 16-channel models. In addition to monitoring consumer loads, it also functions as a smart electricity meter. Through simultaneous energy consumption calculation and power quality analysis, SmartPMS is ideally suited for mission-critical environments such as data centers, large buildings, hospitals, and industrial infrastructures.
Features and Advantages:
Functional Capabilities
-Multi-channel power consumption monitoring (3, 8, and 16 circuits)
-Simultaneous monitoring of current, voltage, power, and energy
-Power Quality Monitoring
-Dual functionality as a multi-circuit meter and smart energy meter
-Real-time detection of electrical anomalies
-Measurement and logging of active, apparent, and reactive energy
-Voltage and current imbalance monitoring
-Over/Under alarms for voltage, current, and frequency
-Auto-range current gain selection
-Manual accuracy adjustment based on CT type
-Modbus RTU communication support
-Suitable for single-phase and three-phase panels
-Compatible with Energy Management Systems and DCIM platforms
Operational Benefits
-Proactive detection of power quality issues before outages occur
-Increased safety and operational continuity of electrical equipment
-Reduced downtime risk in critical infrastructures
-Improved reliability of power distribution networks
Economic Benefits
-Identification of high-consumption loads and energy losses
-Reduced energy and maintenance costs
-Optimized investment in electrical infrastructure
